# README

## Making Files Executable and Running the Program
To run all of the SLURM processes use the quickstart.sh program.
If you want to just build and ready all of the programs but not the SLURM jobs following the following steps with `quickstart_build.sh` insted of `quickstart.sh`
Follow the steps below to make the necessary files executable and run all SLURM the program:

### 1. Make Files Executable
Run the following commands in your terminal to give execute permissions to the required files- NOTE NEED TO CHANGE THIS

```bash
chmod +x quickstart.sh
```

### 2. Run the Program
Run the `quickstart.sh` command in the current directory to run all of the programs:

```bash
./quickstart.sh
```

## After building

After the build was created you can manualy run each test in each program's SLURM using the following command:

```bash
./configs.sh
```



